## To [[make#Verb|make]] (someone or something) [[stormy]]; to [[agitate]] (someone or something) [[violently]].
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Sonnets|poem=A Lover's Complaint|sig=K|verso=1|page=196|passage=And dovvne I laid to liſt the ſad tun'd tale, / Ere long eſpied a fickle maid full pale / Tearing of papers breaking rings a tvvaine, / '''Storming''' her vvorld vvith ſorrovves, vvind and raine.}}
##* {{RQ:Robert Browning La Saisiaz|stanza=64|page=127|passage=Meantime, our simulated thunderclaps / Which tell us counterfeited truths—these same / Are—sound, when music '''storms''' the soul, perhaps?}}
##* {{RQ:Kipling Light that Failed|pages=334–335|pageref=335|passage=The driver turned in the saddle to see if there were any chance of capturing the revolver and ending the ride. Dick roused, struck him over the head with the butt, and '''stormed''' himself wide awake.}}
